# The OpenDubs Authors

"The OpenDubs Authors", the copyright holder named in LICENSE-CODE, LICENSE-HARDWARE,
LICENSE-DOCS and CITATION.cff, are the people listed below.

This file is the one place in the repository where contributors are named on purpose. Everywhere
else, the docs, notes, code and commit messages say "the project team" or "the maintainers".

Emma Romig, project lead

## Being added

You are added only with your own agreement. To be listed, open a pull request that adds one line
in the form `Name, role`, signed off like every other commit (see CONTRIBUTING.md). Ask a
maintainer if you would rather be listed under a handle, or not at all. Contributing does not
require being listed: every signed-off commit is a contribution under the project's licences
either way.
